  "question": {
    "text": "Two parallel long current carrying wire separated by a distance $2 r$ are shown in the figure. The ratio of magnetic field at $A$ to the magnetic field produced at $C$ is $\\frac{x}{7}$. The value of $x$ is _____\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9MS7ZnMVj8mxUk3vMDgjgCcK3kpCiU30-BrkHPcixPY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{B}_{\\mathrm{A}}=\\frac{\\mu_0 \\mathrm{i}}{2 \\pi \\mathrm{r}}+\\frac{\\mu_0(2 \\mathrm{i})}{2 \\pi(3 \\mathrm{r})}=\\frac{5 \\mu_0 \\mathrm{i}}{6 \\pi \\mathrm{r}} \\\\ & \\mathrm{B}_{\\mathrm{C}}=\\frac{\\mu_0(2 \\mathrm{i})}{2 \\pi \\mathrm{r}}+\\frac{\\mu_0 \\mathrm{i}}{2 \\pi(3 \\mathrm{r})}=\\frac{7 \\mu_0 \\mathrm{i}}{6 \\pi \\mathrm{r}} \\\\ & \\therefore \\frac{\\mathrm{B}_{\\mathrm{A}}}{\\mathrm{B}_{\\mathrm{C}}}=\\frac{5}{7} \\\\ & \\therefore \\mathrm{x}=5\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
